# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * the ManageEngine Apache + Notification Server components are started via
#     Start-Service, and dc-run.bat is launched in the BACKGROUND via
#     Start-Process -NoNewWindow, so none of them is PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: ManageEngine Desktop Central is ALREADY RUNNING
# with the vulnerable config, so a fix must restart the affected component
# (safe now - it is not PID 1) for the live checks to pass. Restarting a
# service can never kill the container.
